{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014x3bwb37md4ExqTyaCLBCs","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Median档核心叙事：论文定位为 task formalization + systematic empirical study\n2\t  + bounded claims。 14B结果存在但减弱（68% vs 1B的78%），Claim 1必须从\"robust across scales\"降级为\n3\t  \"feasible at 1B with preliminary evidence of scale persistence at 14B\"。 Binoculars/Fast-DetectGPT\n4\t  ordinal baseline在45-60%的表现削弱方法独特性， 需将优势重新定位为\"systematic multi-model multi-strategy\n5\t  coverage + ordinal-specific feature discovery\"而非单一cell的accuracy优势。 理论section标注为\"Theoretical\n6\t  Motivation\"不列入contribution list。 Cross-strategy pipeline诚实报告strategy classifier瓶颈。\n7\t  论文需要champion reviewer认可problem formalization + Atlas/EDD的价值才能过线。 预期reviewer avg\n8\t  3.0-3.5，borderline accept需要rebuttal中补充14B多策略或调整claim强度。\n9\t\n10\t  '\n11\timagined_experiments:\n12\t- name: 14B_scale_validation\n13\t  plan_id: plan_014\n14\t  description: 'Qwen2.5-14B FP16 + LoRA, nucleus p=0.95, d0-d3递归链。 19特征提取 + RF/LR分类。验证depth\n15\t    signal在14B主流规模下是否持续。\n16\t\n17\t    '\n18\t  expected_results:\n19\t    rf_4class_acc: 0.68\n20\t    rf_4class_ci:\n21\t    - 0.665\n22\t    - 0.695\n23\t    lr_4class_acc: 0.635\n24\t    rf_3class_acc: 0.575\n25\t    d0v1_auc: 0.972\n26\t    d1v2_auc: 0.76\n27\t    d2v3_auc: 0.67\n28\t    d1v3_auc: 0.92\n29\t    per_class_recall_d0: 0.97\n30\t    per_class_recall_d1: 0.72\n31\t    per_class_recall_d2: 0.46\n32\t    per_class_recall_d3: 0.58\n33\t    feature_top4_overlap_with_1b: 2\n34\t    top_features:\n35\t    - p90_ppl\n36\t    - mean_surprisal\n37\t    - type_token_ratio\n38\t    - var_surprisal\n39\t    finetune_loss_d0: 1.85\n40\t    finetune_loss_d1: 1.42\n41\t    finetune_loss_d2: 1.18\n42\t    delta_vs_1b_best_pp: -15.2\n43\t    delta_vs_1b_avg_pp: -11.5\n44\t  result_rationale: '14B模型容量远大于1B，LoRA fine-tune在每一代产生的分布偏移更小—— 模型能更好地在fit训练数据的同时保持生成多样性。具体机制：\n45\t    (1) 14B的attention head冗余度高，LoRA rank=16仅修改极小比例参数， 递归fine-tune对整体生成分布的扰动幅度约为1B的60-70%；\n46\t    (2) perplexity tail statistics (p90_ppl)仍为top feature，因为tail erosion 是recursive\n47\t    generation的universal现象（Shumailov机制与模型规模无关）， 但绝对差异缩小——14B d1的p90_ppl中位数可能在d0和d1之间的gap仅为1B的一半；\n48\t    (3) feature ranking偏移出现在var_surprisal从top-2降至top-4外， 被type_token_ratio替代——14B生成的词汇多样性随depth下降更显著，\n49\t    成为新的discriminative signal； (4) d2 recall最低(46%)，因为14B的d1和d2生成分布高度重叠—— 模型容量使得第2次fine-tune仍能保持较好的生成质量；\n50\t    (5) d0v1 AUC仍然极高(0.97)，因为human text vs任何模型生成的 distinction在任何规模下都很强； (6) fine-tune\n51\t    loss比1B更低（1B约2.2-2.5, 14B约1.85）， 反映14B预训练对训练数据的更好coverage。 整体结果支持\"signal persists\n52\t    but attenuated\"的bounded claim。\n53\t\n54\t    '\n55\t  tables:\n56\t  - name: Table_14B_comparison\n57\t    description: '14B vs 1B三模型对比表：4-class acc, d1v2 AUC, d2v3 AUC, top-4 features。\n58\t      行=模型(Pythia/OLMo/GPT-2 XL/Qwen-14B)，列=metrics。 突出Δ列显示14B的signal attenuation幅度。\n59\t\n60\t      '\n61\t  figures_description:\n62\t  - 'AUC decay curve: x轴=depth pair (d0v1→d2v3), y轴=AUC, 4条线(3个1B模型+14B), 14B线系统性低于1B但保持>0.65'\n63\t  - 'Feature trajectory panel: 14B vs best 1B (GPT-2 XL)的top-5 feature随depth变化, 展示14B\n64\t    feature gap缩小但方向一致'\n65\t  analysis: '68%显著高于chance(25%)，确认14B depth signal存在。但与1B最佳cell(85.4%) 相差17pp，d1v2\n66\t    AUC从0.91降至0.76。论文措辞： \"depth signal persists at 14B scale (68%, chance=25%) but\n67\t    with attenuated inter-depth discrimination (d1v2 AUC 0.76 vs 0.91 at 1B), providing\n68\t    preliminary evidence that the approach extends beyond small models.\" Feature ranking偏移(top-4仅2个重叠)需在paper中显式报告，\n69\t    说明\"feature universality claim需限定为within-scale\"。 这个结果足以消除\"small model only\"的硬伤，但不足以支撑\"scale\n70\t    robust\"的强claim。 审稿人可能要求14B多策略验证(temp09/topk50)作为补充。\n71\t\n72\t    '\n73\t- name: wild_data_calibration\n74\t  plan_id: plan_015\n75\t  description: 'C4/FineWeb/RedPajama子集，GPU reference model特征提取， 3×3训练好的RF分类器做depth预测+分布分析。\n76\t\n77\t    '\n78\t  expected_results:\n79\t    c4_d0_pct: 68.0\n80\t    c4_d1_pct: 28.5\n81\t    c4_d2_pct: 1.8\n82\t    c4_d3_pct: 1.7\n83\t    c4_fpr: 32.0\n84\t    fineweb_d0_pct: 81.0\n85\t    fineweb_d1_pct: 16.5\n86\t    fineweb_d2_pct: 1.2\n87\t    fineweb_d3_pct: 1.3\n88\t    fineweb_fpr: 19.0\n89\t    redpajama_d0_pct: 75.0\n90\t    redpajama_d1_pct: 21.0\n91\t    redpajama_d2_pct: 2.0\n92\t    redpajama_d3_pct: 2.0\n93\t    redpajama_fpr: 25.0\n94\t    cross_model_fpr_std: 8.5\n95\t    wikitext_control_d0_pct: 99.0\n96\t  result_rationale: 'Wild data calibration的核心发现将与已完成的wild_data实验一致但更系统： (1) C4 FPR最高(~32%)因为C4包含大量低质量web-crawl内容——\n97\t    SEO模板、产品描述、自动生成的聚合页面，这些内容的统计特征 (高重复率rep_3gram/rep_4gram、低type_token_ratio、异常p90_ppl)\n98\t    与recursive generation的degradation特征部分重叠； (2) FineWeb FPR较低(~19%)因为FineWeb经过质量过滤，\n99\t    但仍有template-like内容导致false positives； (3) RedPajama是新测试集，预期FPR在C4和FineWeb之间(~25%)，\n100\t    因为RedPajama的数据来源多样(CommonCrawl+Wikipedia+Books等)， CommonCrawl部分贡献高FPR，Wikipedia/Books部分贡献低FPR；\n101\t    (4) 所有d2+/d3+误分类极少(<3%)——wild data被误分为deep recursive的 概率极低，绝大多数false positives是d0→d1的轻度误分；\n102\t    (5) WikiText控制组保持~99% d0，确认高质量editorial text不受影响； (6) cross-model FPR variance(std~8.5pp)反映不同reference\n103\t    model的 特征空间差异——Pythia reference vs GPT-2 XL reference给出的FPR可能 差10+pp，因为reference\n104\t    model的perplexity baseline影响特征分布。 这个variance是paper必须报告的limitation。\n105\t\n106\t    '\n107\t  tables:\n108\t  - name: Table_wild_data_depth_distribution\n109\t    description: '行=数据集(C4/FineWeb/RedPajama/WikiText-control/OpenWebText-control),\n110\t      列=predicted depth分布(d0%/d1%/d2%/d3%)+FPR+N。 附注：FPR定义为non-d0 predictions在已知human-text数据集上的比例。\n111\t\n112\t      '\n113\t  figures_description:\n114\t  - 'Feature distribution shift: 核心特征(p90_ppl, var_surprisal, rep_4gram)在controlled\n115\t    d0 vs wild d0 vs wild FP的kernel density plot, 展示FP样本与template/SEO content的特征重叠'\n116\t  analysis: 'Wild data结果支持\"depth signal is detectable in controlled settings, with\n117\t    web-crawl domain shift as a known limitation\"的narrative。 ~20-32% FPR在web-crawl上看起来高，但(a)\n118\t    全部集中在d0→d1轻度误分， (b) FP内容inspect后是template/SEO而非random noise， (c) high-quality\n119\t    editorial data FPR<2%。 论文应在Limitations中明确写：\"deployment on web-crawl data requires\n120\t    a domain-adapted threshold or supplementary quality filter to reduce FPR from\n121\t    template content.\" 审稿人可能要求FPR的systematic analysis（已有数据支持）。\n122\t\n123\t    '\n124\t- name: detector_ordinal_baseline\n125\t  plan_id: plan_018\n126\t  description: 'Binoculars + Fast-DetectGPT连续分数校准为ordinal depth bin， 在3×3矩阵已有数据上评估4-class\n127\t    ordinal accuracy。\n128\t\n129\t    '\n130\t  expected_results:\n131\t    binoculars_4class_acc_mean: 0.48\n132\t    binoculars_4class_acc_range:\n133\t    - 0.42\n134\t    - 0.56\n135\t    binoculars_d0v1_auc: 0.965\n136\t    binoculars_d1v2_auc: 0.61\n137\t    binoculars_d2v3_auc: 0.54\n138\t    binoculars_best_cell: gpt2xl_temp09\n139\t    binoculars_best_cell_acc: 0.56\n140\t    binoculars_worst_cell: pythia_topk50\n141\t    binoculars_worst_cell_acc: 0.42\n142\t    fastdetectgpt_4class_acc_mean: 0.54\n143\t    fastdetectgpt_4class_acc_range:\n144\t    - 0.47\n145\t    - 0.6\n146\t    fastdetectgpt_d0v1_auc: 0.975\n147\t    fastdetectgpt_d1v2_auc: 0.66\n148\t    fastdetectgpt_d2v3_auc: 0.57\n149\t    fastdetectgpt_best_cell: gpt2xl_temp09\n150\t    fastdetectgpt_best_cell_acc: 0.6\n151\t    fastdetectgpt_worst_cell: pythia_topk50\n152\t    fastdetectgpt_worst_cell_acc: 0.47\n153\t    gap_vs_rf_mean_pp: 25.0\n154\t    gap_vs_rf_on_topk50_pp: 12.0\n155\t    detector_3class_acc_mean: 0.41\n156\t  result_rationale: 'Binoculars/Fast-DetectGPT设计目标是binary real-vs-synthetic detection，\n157\t    其连续分数编码了text的\"synthetic-ness\"程度但不是ordinal depth gradient： (1) d0v1 AUC极高(0.96-0.98)——这正是这些检测器的设计强项，\n158\t    human text vs 任何深度的synthetic text的boundary它们捕捉得很好； (2) d1v2和d2v3 AUC急剧下降(0.61-0.66,\n159\t    0.54-0.57)—— 这些检测器的score在d1/d2/d3上趋于饱和，因为从binary视角看 d1/d2/d3都是\"synthetic\"，score的微小差异不足以支撑ordinal\n160\t    ranking； (3) Fast-DetectGPT略优于Binoculars(+6pp)因为其概率曲率估计 对distribution tail更敏感，与depth\n161\t    degradation的tail erosion机制 有间接对齐； (4) 最佳cell (gpt2xl_temp09, 60%)接近我们的topk50弱cell(69.6%)，\n162\t    gap仅~10pp——这是reviewer质疑method novelty的弹药； (5) 3-class accuracy(排除d0)骤降至~41%，因为去掉最容易的d0类后，\n163\t    detectors在pure ordinal任务上接近chance(33%)； (6) 按cell分析，detector在topk50设置上表现最接近我们的方法，\n164\t    因为topk50本身信号弱，我们的feature-based方法也没有大优势。 这个baseline的存在要求论文narrative从\"我们的方法优于existing\n165\t    detectors\" 转向\"existing detectors retain partial ordinal signal but lack the systematic\n166\t    coverage and feature-level understanding we provide\"。\n167\t\n168\t    '\n169\t  tables:\n170\t  - name: Table_detector_ordinal_comparison\n171\t    description: '行=方法(RF-19feat/CORAL/DivEye/Binoculars/Fast-DetectGPT/Chance), 列=9个cells的4-class\n172\t      acc + mean + 3-class mean。 最后两列=d1v2 AUC mean和d2v3 AUC mean。 加粗每列最高值。RF-19feat在8/9\n173\t      cells最高， 但Binoculars/FDGPT在topk50 cells接近。\n174\t\n175\t      '\n176\t  figures_description:\n177\t  - '方法对比bar chart: 9 cells × 6 methods的4-class acc grouped bar chart, 直观显示RF/CORAL/DivEye的优势在temp09/nucleus\n178\t    cells上最大, 在topk50 cells上缩小'\n179\t  - 'AUC decay对比: d0v1→d2v3的AUC decay curve, RF vs Binoculars vs Fast-DetectGPT, 展示detectors在d0v1接近RF但在deeper\n180\t    pairs急剧下降'\n181\t  analysis: 'Detector ordinal baseline的结果是双刃剑： 正面——确认ordinal depth estimation不是trivial的(detectors\n182\t    <60%)， 我们的方法有15-25pp优势(mean)； 负面——在topk50弱cell上gap缩小到~10pp，且Fast-DetectGPT的60%\n183\t    在absolute terms不低。论文必须诚实报告并重新定位优势： \"Our feature-based approach provides 15-25pp\n184\t    improvement over calibrated binary detectors on average, with the largest gains\n185\t    in higher-signal settings (nucleus, temp09). The gap narrows for topk50, where\n186\t    both approaches struggle with attenuated signal.\" 审稿人可能认为这表明\"feature engineering的marginal\n187\t    gain不够justify a full paper\"——rebuttal需强调Atlas/EDD/feature universality finding\n188\t    才是contribution，method accuracy是supporting evidence。\n189\t\n190\t    '\n191\t- name: bootstrap_confidence_intervals\n192\t  plan_id: plan_020\n193\t  description: '9个3×3 cells的5-fold CV bootstrap 95% CI计算，用于Table 1报告。\n194\t\n195\t    '\n196\t  expected_results:\n197\t    ci_width_mean_pp: 1.8\n198\t    ci_width_range_pp:\n199\t    - 1.2\n200\t    - 2.8\n201\t    gpt2xl_temp09_ci:\n202\t    - 0.843\n203\t    - 0.866\n204\t    gpt2xl_nucleus_ci:\n205\t    - 0.828\n206\t    - 0.851\n207\t    olmo_temp09_ci:\n208\t    - 0.812\n209\t    - 0.84\n210\t    olmo_nucleus_ci:\n211\t    - 0.776\n212\t    - 0.803\n213\t    pythia_nucleus_ci:\n214\t    - 0.768\n215\t    - 0.795\n216\t    pythia_temp09_ci:\n217\t    - 0.749\n218\t    - 0.776\n219\t    olmo_topk50_ci:\n220\t    - 0.728\n221\t    - 0.758\n222\t    pythia_topk50_ci:\n223\t    - 0.681\n224\t    - 0.711\n225\t    gpt2xl_topk50_ci:\n226\t    - 0.743\n227\t    - 0.77\n228\t    overlapping_pairs: 3\n229\t    all_above_chance: true\n230\t  result_rationale: 'Bootstrap CI宽度由样本量和fold间variance决定： (1) 每个cell约20000 samples\n231\t    (5000/depth), 5-fold CV的fold间 variance较小(std ~2-3pp), bootstrap 95% CI宽度在1.2-2.8pp；\n232\t    (2) 高accuracy cells (gpt2xl_temp09 85.4%)的CI更窄(~2.2pp) 因为接近ceiling时variance更小；\n233\t    (3) 中等accuracy cells (pythia_topk50 69.6%)的CI稍宽(~2.8pp) 因为错误率更高导致更大variance； (4)\n234\t    约3对adjacent cells有CI重叠(如olmo_nucleus vs pythia_nucleus, gpt2xl_topk50 vs pythia_temp09)——这些重叠不影响main\n235\t    claims 因为跨model比较不是core claim； (5) 所有9个cells的CI下界都远高于chance(25%)，最低的 pythia_topk50下界约68.1%，支撑\"well\n236\t    above chance\"的claim。\n237\t\n238\t    '\n239\t  tables:\n240\t  - name: Table_1_with_CIs\n241\t    description: '标准3×3 Table 1更新版：行=model(Pythia/OLMo/GPT-2 XL), 列=strategy(nucleus/temp09/topk50)。\n242\t      每个cell显示\"acc% [CI_low, CI_high]\"。附行均值和列均值。\n243\t\n244\t      '\n245\t  figures_description: []\n246\t  analysis: 'Bootstrap CI是paper reporting质量的基本要求，审稿人三档均要求。 主要作用：(1) 证明所有cells统计显著高于chance；\n247\t    (2) topk50的CI可能被reviewer用来argue\"weakest setting接近 baseline\"——但CI下界仍在68%以上； (3)\n248\t    部分cells间CI重叠说明model effect和strategy effect的 大小关系需要在paper中显式讨论。\n249\t\n250\t    '\n251\t- name: theoretical_analysis_section\n252\t  plan_id: plan_023\n253\t  description: '理论分析section：(1) tail erosion连接p90_ppl/var_surprisal, (2) EDD上界推导,\n254\t    (3) strategy-dependent convergence rate解释。\n255\t\n256\t    '\n257\t  expected_results:\n258\t    tail_erosion_connection: qualitative — links p90_ppl dominance to Shumailov 2024\n259\t      tail collapse mechanism\n260\t    edd_upper_bound_formula: EDD ≤ ⌈log(D_KL(P_0 || P_ref) / τ_disc) / log(1/γ)⌉ where\n261\t      γ is contraction rate\n262\t    edd_bound_empirical_match: bound gives EDD≤6 for 1B models, empirical EDD=4 —\n263\t      bound is loose but directionally correct\n264\t    iid_assumption_violation: acknowledged — LoRA recursive chain violates i.i.d.\n265\t      because each depth uses different LoRA weights\n266\t    strategy_convergence_explanation: temperature uniform scaling accelerates KL contraction\n267\t      by factor ~1.3-1.5x vs truncation methods\n268\t    section_length_pages: 1.5\n269\t    contribution_list_included: false\n270\t    section_label: Theoretical Motivation\n271\t  result_rationale: '理论section在median档下仅提供定性连接： (1) Tail erosion连接：Shumailov et al.\n272\t    2024证明recursive training 使模型逐渐丧失对低概率token的生成能力(tail collapse)， 这直接解释了为什么p90_ppl(捕捉高perplexity\n273\t    tail)和var_surprisal (捕捉surprisal分布宽度)是universal top features—— recursive generation系统性地压缩perplexity分布的right\n274\t    tail， 使p90_ppl单调下降。这个连接是直觉性的、定性的，不构成新理论； (2) EDD上界推导：假设recursive generation是contraction\n275\t    mapping (每代分布向attractor收敛，contraction rate γ<1)， EDD是相邻depths的KL divergence首次降至discriminability\n276\t    threshold τ_disc以下的depth。推导得EDD ≤ ⌈log(D_0/τ)/log(1/γ)⌉。 问题：此推导假设i.i.d. generation（每代用同一个generative\n277\t    process）， 但实际实验中每个depth用不同的LoRA checkpoint—— 审稿人会指出\"the bound assumes a fixed\n278\t    contraction operator, but your LoRA fine-tuning creates a different operator at\n279\t    each depth\"； (3) EDD bound给出≤6（1B模型），empirical EDD=4—— bound是loose的但方向正确，审稿人可能认为\"a\n280\t    bound that overestimates by 50% is descriptive rather than tight\"； (4) Strategy\n281\t    convergence rate解释：temperature对logit做uniform scaling (除以τ)保持分布shape但改变entropy，而nucleus/topk做truncation\n282\t    (截断低概率tail)。Temperature使模型更快收敛到uniform-like attractor， 解释了temp09的d1→d2 feature\n283\t    trajectory reversal。 这个解释有mechanistic basis但缺乏formal proof； (5) 整个section约1.5页，标注为\"Theoretical\n284\t    Motivation\"， 不列入contribution list以避免审稿人的\"no theoretical contribution\"critique。\n285\t\n286\t    '\n287\t  tables: []\n288\t  figures_description:\n289\t  - 'EDD bound vs empirical: 柱状图showing theoretical upper bound (6) vs empirical EDD\n290\t    at T=0.75 across 3 models (all=4), 附contraction rate γ估计值'\n291\t  - 'Tail erosion visualization: p90_ppl的empirical CDF across depths (d0-d3), 展示right\n292\t    tail系统性左移, 连接到Shumailov tail collapse theory'\n293\t  analysis: 'Median档下理论section的定位是\"adds motivation but not substance\"。 审稿人典型反应：\"The\n294\t    theoretical sketch is helpful for intuition but the EDD bound relies on assumptions\n295\t    that don''t hold in practice (i.i.d. generation). I appreciate the connection\n296\t    to model collapse theory but would categorize this as ''descriptive'' rather than\n297\t    ''a theoretical contribution''.\" 这意味着理论section不会提升reviewer score，但也不会扣分—— 它防止了\"no\n298\t    theoretical grounding at all\"的批评。 关键是不要oversell：paper说\"we provide theoretical\n299\t    motivation connecting our empirical findings to model collapse theory\" 而非\"we derive\n300\t    novel theoretical results\"。\n301\t\n302\t    '\n303\t- name: api_model_recursive_chains\n304\t  plan_id: plan_026\n305\t  description: 'GPT-4o-mini fine-tuning API递归链 + prompted recursive chain (rewrite模式)，\n306\t    验证depth signal在商用API模型中的存在性。\n307\t\n308\t    '\n309\t  expected_results:\n310\t    prompted_chain_4class_acc: 0.42\n311\t    prompted_chain_d0v1_auc: 0.73\n312\t    prompted_chain_d1v2_auc: 0.57\n313\t    prompted_chain_d2v3_auc: 0.52\n314\t    prompted_chain_top_features:\n315\t    - surprisal_range\n316\t    - prob_std\n317\t    - var_surprisal\n318\t    finetuned_chain_feasibility: limited — API fine-tuning constraints (no LoRA control,\n319\t      fixed epochs) make recursive chain less controlled\n320\t    finetuned_chain_4class_acc: 0.45\n321\t    finetuned_chain_d1v2_auc: 0.59\n322\t    delta_vs_base_1b_pp: -36.0\n323\t    delta_vs_instruct_pp: -3.0\n324\t  result_rationale: 'API模型结果弱于base model，与instruct model实验(plan_021, 47.4%)一致： (1)\n325\t    Prompted recursive chain (rewrite prompting)：每次\"rewrite\"不等同于 LoRA fine-tune——fine-tune改变模型参数使分布永久偏移，\n326\t    prompted rewrite仅在inference时施加instruction bias。 因此递归prompted generation的分布偏移幅度远小于LoRA递归链，\n327\t    导致相邻depth的statistical features差异更小； (2) API fine-tuning (GPT-4o-mini)：OpenAI fine-tuning\n328\t    API不暴露 LoRA rank/learning rate等超参数，默认训练3 epochs且有 内置regularization防止catastrophic\n329\t    forgetting—— 这正是depth signal所需要的分布偏移的对立面。 递归fine-tune在API上产生的每代偏移可能仅为本地LoRA的30-40%；\n330\t    (3) RLHF/instruction tuning引入的分布约束(alignment tax) 使模型生成更\"standardized\"——不同depth的生成在style/fluency上更一致，\n331\t    压缩了statistical feature的variance； (4) Feature ranking偏移：p90_ppl不再dominant(被surprisal_range替代)，\n332\t    因为API模型的perplexity tail被RLHF regularize过， tail erosion信号被alignment process预先消除；\n333\t    (5) 42-45%的accuracy仍高于chance(25%)，说明signal exists but is weak—— 这支撑\"depth signal\n334\t    is strongest in base models at moderate scale\" 的bounded claim。\n335\t\n336\t    '\n337\t  tables:\n338\t  - name: Table_model_type_comparison\n339\t    description: '行=模型类型(Base 1B avg / Base 14B / Instruct 1.5B / API prompted / API\n340\t      finetuned), 列=4class acc / d1v2 AUC / d0v1 AUC / top feature。 展示signal strength随model\n341\t      regularization递减的gradient。\n342\t\n343\t      '\n344\t  figures_description:\n345\t  - 'Signal strength gradient: 条形图showing 4-class acc across model types (base→instruct→API),\n346\t    展示从78%→47%→42%的递减趋势'\n347\t  analysis: 'API模型结果确认\"depth signal is a property of base model generation that is\n348\t    attenuated by instruction tuning and RLHF alignment\"。 论文framing：depth estimation\n349\t    is most applicable to base model outputs in data feedback loops (the primary use\n350\t    case), while instruct/API model chains show attenuated but non-zero signal. 审稿人可能将此解读为limitation(\"only\n351\t    works well on base models\") 或strength(\"correctly identifies that aligned models\n352\t    resist distributional drift\")——取决于reviewer perspective。 Median档下至少一位审稿人会用这个结果argue\n353\t    \"practical impact is limited since most real-world synthetic text comes from instruct/API\n354\t    models\"。\n355\t\n356\t    '\n357\t- name: dcol_component_ablation\n358\t  plan_id: plan_010\n359\t  description: DCOL组件消融实验——已取消，因前置条件plan_004(DCOL v6)结论为negative。\n360\t  expected_results:\n361\t    status: cancelled\n362\t    reason: DCOL v6 RoBERTa-large failed (64.4% vs RF 78.2%, -13.7pp, severe overfitting).\n363\t      No DCOL model to ablate.\n364\t  result_rationale: 'DCOL v1-v6全部失败表明contrastive ordinal learning在text depth estimation\n365\t    任务上有固有困难：(1) 文本的ordinal depth signal主要编码在statistical features (perplexity tail,\n366\t    surprisal variance)中，而非token-level embeddings能直接捕捉的； (2) contrastive loss需要embedding空间中adjacent\n367\t    depths有清晰的ordinal structure， 但RoBERTa的[CLS] embedding捕捉的是语义信息而非distributional\n368\t    statistics； (3) 这个negative result本身支持Atlas/EDD作为primary contribution的定位—— 表明depth\n369\t    estimation的贡献在于feature discovery和task formalization， 而非novel deep learning architecture。\n370\t\n371\t    '\n372\t  tables: []\n373\t  figures_description: []\n374\t  analysis: 'Plan_010取消不影响论文结构。DCOL negative result已纳入paper的 negative analysis section\n375\t    (Section 5或Appendix)， 作为\"contrastive ordinal learning的固有局限\"discussion。\n376\t\n377\t    '\n378\t- name: theory_section_whatif\n379\t  plan_id: what_if:theory_section\n380\t  description: '与plan_023重叠的theoretical analysis what-if。 在median档下评估其对reviewer score的marginal\n381\t    impact。\n382\t\n383\t    '\n384\t  expected_results:\n385\t    marginal_score_impact: +0.0 to +0.25\n386\t    reviewer_perception: appreciated as motivation, not counted as contribution\n387\t    best_case: reviewer says 'nice connection to theory, strengthens the empirical\n388\t      narrative'\n389\t    worst_case: reviewer says 'the theoretical analysis is superficial and the EDD\n390\t      bound is too loose to be useful'\n391\t    champion_reviewer_probability: 0.35\n392\t  result_rationale: '理论section在median档的marginal impact接近零到微正： (1) 正面场景(+0.25)：某位reviewer认可problem\n393\t    formalization +  theoretical motivation的组合，认为\"this paper doesn''t need novel theory\n394\t    to be valuable — the empirical contribution is sufficient, and the theoretical\n395\t    sketch adds context\"； (2) 中性场景(+0.0)：reviewer认为理论section是nice-to-have但 不改变evaluation——\"the\n396\t    theory section provides some intuition but doesn''t affect my assessment of the\n397\t    empirical claims\"； (3) 微负场景(-0.1)：aggressive reviewer认为理论section raises expectations\n398\t    it doesn''t meet——\"including a ''theory'' section suggests the authors believe\n399\t    they have a theoretical contribution, but the analysis is too informal to qualify\"。\n400\t    Median档的结果是(2)或(1)，取决于reviewer composition。 Champion reviewer(认可formalization价值)的概率约35%——\n401\t    需要恰好分配到有empirical study appreciation的reviewer。\n402\t\n403\t    '\n404\t  tables: []\n405\t  figures_description: []\n406\t  analysis: Theory section是low-risk low-reward的addition。 在median档下它不会pushing the paper\n407\t    from 3.0 to 3.5， 但也不会hurt。其主要价值是在rebuttal中当reviewer问 \"why these features?\"时可以指向theory\n408\t    section作为解释。 建议：保留theory section但严格控制scope和claim， 明确标注为\"Theoretical Motivation\"并在Introduction的\n409\t    contribution list中不单独列出。\n410\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"54767580-3114-45ce-b1df-d1aec2ac2b43","uuid":"f840185e-3a38-4bfa-9d37-cbad70a98f0f","timestamp":"2026-05-18T17:00:41.756Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_2/projects/recursive_gen_depth_est/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260518T162616/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'Median档核心叙事：论文定位为 task formalization + systematic empirical study\n  + bounded claims。 14B结果存在但减弱（68% vs 1B的78%），Claim 1必须从\"robust across scales\"降级为\n  \"feasible at 1B with preliminary evidence of scale persistence at 14B\"。 Binoculars/Fast-DetectGPT\n  ordinal baseline在45-60%的表现削弱方法独特性， 需将优势重新定位为\"systematic multi-model multi-strategy\n  coverage + ordinal-specific feature discovery\"而非单一cell的accuracy优势。 理论section标注为\"Theoretical\n  Motivation\"不列入contribution list。 Cross-strategy pipeline诚实报告strategy classifier瓶颈。\n  论文需要champion reviewer认可problem formalization + Atlas/EDD的价值才能过线。 预期reviewer avg\n  3.0-3.5，borderline accept需要rebuttal中补充14B多策略或调整claim强度。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: 14B_scale_validation\n  plan_id: plan_014\n  description: 'Qwen2.5-14B FP16 + LoRA, nucleus p=0.95, d0-d3递归链。 19特征提取 + RF/LR分类。验证depth\n    signal在14B主流规模下是否持续。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    rf_4class_acc: 0.68\n    rf_4class_ci:\n    - 0.665\n    - 0.695\n    lr_4class_acc: 0.635\n    rf_3class_acc: 0.575\n    d0v1_auc: 0.972\n    d1v2_auc: 0.76\n    d2v3_auc: 0.67\n    d1v3_auc: 0.92\n    per_class_recall_d0: 0.97\n    per_class_recall_d1: 0.72\n    per_class_recall_d2: 0.46\n    per_class_recall_d3: 0.58\n    feature_top4_overlap_with_1b: 2\n    top_features:\n    - p90_ppl\n    - mean_surprisal\n    - type_token_ratio\n    - var_surprisal\n    finetune_loss_d0: 1.85\n    finetune_loss_d1: 1.42\n    finetune_loss_d2: 1.18\n    delta_vs_1b_best_pp: -15.2\n    delta_vs_1b_avg_pp: -11.5\n  result_rationale: '14B模型容量远大于1B，LoRA fine-tune在每一代产生的分布偏移更小—— 模型能更好地在fit训练数据的同时保持生成多样性。具体机制：\n    (1) 14B的attention head冗余度高，LoRA rank=16仅修改极小比例参数， 递归fine-tune对整体生成分布的扰动幅度约为1B的60-70%；\n    (2) perplexity tail statistics (p90_ppl)仍为top feature，因为tail erosion 是recursive\n    generation的universal现象（Shumailov机制与模型规模无关）， 但绝对差异缩小——14B d1的p90_ppl中位数可能在d0和d1之间的gap仅为1B的一半；\n    (3) feature ranking偏移出现在var_surprisal从top-2降至top-4外， 被type_token_ratio替代——14B生成的词汇多样性随depth下降更显著，\n    成为新的discriminative signal； (4) d2 recall最低(46%)，因为14B的d1和d2生成分布高度重叠—— 模型容量使得第2次fine-tune仍能保持较好的生成质量；\n    (5) d0v1 AUC仍然极高(0.97)，因为human text vs任何模型生成的 distinction在任何规模下都很强； (6) fine-tune\n    loss比1B更低（1B约2.2-2.5, 14B约1.85）， 反映14B预训练对训练数据的更好coverage。 整体结果支持\"signal persists\n    but attenuated\"的bounded claim。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Table_14B_comparison\n    description: '14B vs 1B三模型对比表：4-class acc, d1v2 AUC, d2v3 AUC, top-4 features。\n      行=模型(Pythia/OLMo/GPT-2 XL/Qwen-14B)，列=metrics。 突出Δ列显示14B的signal attenuation幅度。\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'AUC decay curve: x轴=depth pair (d0v1→d2v3), y轴=AUC, 4条线(3个1B模型+14B), 14B线系统性低于1B但保持>0.65'\n  - 'Feature trajectory panel: 14B vs best 1B (GPT-2 XL)的top-5 feature随depth变化, 展示14B\n    feature gap缩小但方向一致'\n  analysis: '68%显著高于chance(25%)，确认14B depth signal存在。但与1B最佳cell(85.4%) 相差17pp，d1v2\n    AUC从0.91降至0.76。论文措辞： \"depth signal persists at 14B scale (68%, chance=25%) but\n    with attenuated inter-depth discrimination (d1v2 AUC 0.76 vs 0.91 at 1B), providing\n    preliminary evidence that the approach extends beyond small models.\" Feature ranking偏移(top-4仅2个重叠)需在paper中显式报告，\n    说明\"feature universality claim需限定为within-scale\"。 这个结果足以消除\"small model only\"的硬伤，但不足以支撑\"scale\n    robust\"的强claim。 审稿人可能要求14B多策略验证(temp09/topk50)作为补充。\n\n    '\n- name: wild_data_calibration\n  plan_id: plan_015\n  description: 'C4/FineWeb/RedPajama子集，GPU reference model特征提取， 3×3训练好的RF分类器做depth预测+分布分析。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    c4_d0_pct: 68.0\n    c4_d1_pct: 28.5\n    c4_d2_pct: 1.8\n    c4_d3_pct: 1.7\n    c4_fpr: 32.0\n    fineweb_d0_pct: 81.0\n    fineweb_d1_pct: 16.5\n    fineweb_d2_pct: 1.2\n    fineweb_d3_pct: 1.3\n    fineweb_fpr: 19.0\n    redpajama_d0_pct: 75.0\n    redpajama_d1_pct: 21.0\n    redpajama_d2_pct: 2.0\n    redpajama_d3_pct: 2.0\n    redpajama_fpr: 25.0\n    cross_model_fpr_std: 8.5\n    wikitext_control_d0_pct: 99.0\n  result_rationale: 'Wild data calibration的核心发现将与已完成的wild_data实验一致但更系统： (1) C4 FPR最高(~32%)因为C4包含大量低质量web-crawl内容——\n    SEO模板、产品描述、自动生成的聚合页面，这些内容的统计特征 (高重复率rep_3gram/rep_4gram、低type_token_ratio、异常p90_ppl)\n    与recursive generation的degradation特征部分重叠； (2) FineWeb FPR较低(~19%)因为FineWeb经过质量过滤，\n    但仍有template-like内容导致false positives； (3) RedPajama是新测试集，预期FPR在C4和FineWeb之间(~25%)，\n    因为RedPajama的数据来源多样(CommonCrawl+Wikipedia+Books等)， CommonCrawl部分贡献高FPR，Wikipedia/Books部分贡献低FPR；\n    (4) 所有d2+/d3+误分类极少(<3%)——wild data被误分为deep recursive的 概率极低，绝大多数false positives是d0→d1的轻度误分；\n    (5) WikiText控制组保持~99% d0，确认高质量editorial text不受影响； (6) cross-model FPR variance(std~8.5pp)反映不同reference\n    model的 特征空间差异——Pythia reference vs GPT-2 XL reference给出的FPR可能 差10+pp，因为reference\n    model的perplexity baseline影响特征分布。 这个variance是paper必须报告的limitation。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Table_wild_data_depth_distribution\n    description: '行=数据集(C4/FineWeb/RedPajama/WikiText-control/OpenWebText-control),\n      列=predicted depth分布(d0%/d1%/d2%/d3%)+FPR+N。 附注：FPR定义为non-d0 predictions在已知human-text数据集上的比例。\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Feature distribution shift: 核心特征(p90_ppl, var_surprisal, rep_4gram)在controlled\n    d0 vs wild d0 vs wild FP的kernel density plot, 展示FP样本与template/SEO content的特征重叠'\n  analysis: 'Wild data结果支持\"depth signal is detectable in controlled settings, with\n    web-crawl domain shift as a known limitation\"的narrative。 ~20-32% FPR在web-crawl上看起来高，但(a)\n    全部集中在d0→d1轻度误分， (b) FP内容inspect后是template/SEO而非random noise， (c) high-quality\n    editorial data FPR<2%。 论文应在Limitations中明确写：\"deployment on web-crawl data requires\n    a domain-adapted threshold or supplementary quality filter to reduce FPR from\n    template content.\" 审稿人可能要求FPR的systematic analysis（已有数据支持）。\n\n    '\n- name: detector_ordinal_baseline\n  plan_id: plan_018\n  description: 'Binoculars + Fast-DetectGPT连续分数校准为ordinal depth bin， 在3×3矩阵已有数据上评估4-class\n    ordinal accuracy。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    binoculars_4class_acc_mean: 0.48\n    binoculars_4class_acc_range:\n    - 0.42\n    - 0.56\n    binoculars_d0v1_auc: 0.965\n    binoculars_d1v2_auc: 0.61\n    binoculars_d2v3_auc: 0.54\n    binoculars_best_cell: gpt2xl_temp09\n    binoculars_best_cell_acc: 0.56\n    binoculars_worst_cell: pythia_topk50\n    binoculars_worst_cell_acc: 0.42\n    fastdetectgpt_4class_acc_mean: 0.54\n    fastdetectgpt_4class_acc_range:\n    - 0.47\n    - 0.6\n    fastdetectgpt_d0v1_auc: 0.975\n    fastdetectgpt_d1v2_auc: 0.66\n    fastdetectgpt_d2v3_auc: 0.57\n    fastdetectgpt_best_cell: gpt2xl_temp09\n    fastdetectgpt_best_cell_acc: 0.6\n    fastdetectgpt_worst_cell: pythia_topk50\n    fastdetectgpt_worst_cell_acc: 0.47\n    gap_vs_rf_mean_pp: 25.0\n    gap_vs_rf_on_topk50_pp: 12.0\n    detector_3class_acc_mean: 0.41\n  result_rationale: 'Binoculars/Fast-DetectGPT设计目标是binary real-vs-synthetic detection，\n    其连续分数编码了text的\"synthetic-ness\"程度但不是ordinal depth gradient： (1) d0v1 AUC极高(0.96-0.98)——这正是这些检测器的设计强项，\n    human text vs 任何深度的synthetic text的boundary它们捕捉得很好； (2) d1v2和d2v3 AUC急剧下降(0.61-0.66,\n    0.54-0.57)—— 这些检测器的score在d1/d2/d3上趋于饱和，因为从binary视角看 d1/d2/d3都是\"synthetic\"，score的微小差异不足以支撑ordinal\n    ranking； (3) Fast-DetectGPT略优于Binoculars(+6pp)因为其概率曲率估计 对distribution tail更敏感，与depth\n    degradation的tail erosion机制 有间接对齐； (4) 最佳cell (gpt2xl_temp09, 60%)接近我们的topk50弱cell(69.6%)，\n    gap仅~10pp——这是reviewer质疑method novelty的弹药； (5) 3-class accuracy(排除d0)骤降至~41%，因为去掉最容易的d0类后，\n    detectors在pure ordinal任务上接近chance(33%)； (6) 按cell分析，detector在topk50设置上表现最接近我们的方法，\n    因为topk50本身信号弱，我们的feature-based方法也没有大优势。 这个baseline的存在要求论文narrative从\"我们的方法优于existing\n    detectors\" 转向\"existing detectors retain partial ordinal signal but lack the systematic\n    coverage and feature-level understanding we provide\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Table_detector_ordinal_comparison\n    description: '行=方法(RF-19feat/CORAL/DivEye/Binoculars/Fast-DetectGPT/Chance), 列=9个cells的4-class\n      acc + mean + 3-class mean。 最后两列=d1v2 AUC mean和d2v3 AUC mean。 加粗每列最高值。RF-19feat在8/9\n      cells最高， 但Binoculars/FDGPT在topk50 cells接近。\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - '方法对比bar chart: 9 cells × 6 methods的4-class acc grouped bar chart, 直观显示RF/CORAL/DivEye的优势在temp09/nucleus\n    cells上最大, 在topk50 cells上缩小'\n  - 'AUC decay对比: d0v1→d2v3的AUC decay curve, RF vs Binoculars vs Fast-DetectGPT, 展示detectors在d0v1接近RF但在deeper\n    pairs急剧下降'\n  analysis: 'Detector ordinal baseline的结果是双刃剑： 正面——确认ordinal depth estimation不是trivial的(detectors\n    <60%)， 我们的方法有15-25pp优势(mean)； 负面——在topk50弱cell上gap缩小到~10pp，且Fast-DetectGPT的60%\n    在absolute terms不低。论文必须诚实报告并重新定位优势： \"Our feature-based approach provides 15-25pp\n    improvement over calibrated binary detectors on average, with the largest gains\n    in higher-signal settings (nucleus, temp09). The gap narrows for topk50, where\n    both approaches struggle with attenuated signal.\" 审稿人可能认为这表明\"feature engineering的marginal\n    gain不够justify a full paper\"——rebuttal需强调Atlas/EDD/feature universality finding\n    才是contribution，method accuracy是supporting evidence。\n\n    '\n- name: bootstrap_confidence_intervals\n  plan_id: plan_020\n  description: '9个3×3 cells的5-fold CV bootstrap 95% CI计算，用于Table 1报告。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    ci_width_mean_pp: 1.8\n    ci_width_range_pp:\n    - 1.2\n    - 2.8\n    gpt2xl_temp09_ci:\n    - 0.843\n    - 0.866\n    gpt2xl_nucleus_ci:\n    - 0.828\n    - 0.851\n    olmo_temp09_ci:\n    - 0.812\n    - 0.84\n    olmo_nucleus_ci:\n    - 0.776\n    - 0.803\n    pythia_nucleus_ci:\n    - 0.768\n    - 0.795\n    pythia_temp09_ci:\n    - 0.749\n    - 0.776\n    olmo_topk50_ci:\n    - 0.728\n    - 0.758\n    pythia_topk50_ci:\n    - 0.681\n    - 0.711\n    gpt2xl_topk50_ci:\n    - 0.743\n    - 0.77\n    overlapping_pairs: 3\n    all_above_chance: true\n  result_rationale: 'Bootstrap CI宽度由样本量和fold间variance决定： (1) 每个cell约20000 samples\n    (5000/depth), 5-fold CV的fold间 variance较小(std ~2-3pp), bootstrap 95% CI宽度在1.2-2.8pp；\n    (2) 高accuracy cells (gpt2xl_temp09 85.4%)的CI更窄(~2.2pp) 因为接近ceiling时variance更小；\n    (3) 中等accuracy cells (pythia_topk50 69.6%)的CI稍宽(~2.8pp) 因为错误率更高导致更大variance； (4)\n    约3对adjacent cells有CI重叠(如olmo_nucleus vs pythia_nucleus, gpt2xl_topk50 vs pythia_temp09)——这些重叠不影响main\n    claims 因为跨model比较不是core claim； (5) 所有9个cells的CI下界都远高于chance(25%)，最低的 pythia_topk50下界约68.1%，支撑\"well\n    above chance\"的claim。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Table_1_with_CIs\n    description: '标准3×3 Table 1更新版：行=model(Pythia/OLMo/GPT-2 XL), 列=strategy(nucleus/temp09/topk50)。\n      每个cell显示\"acc% [CI_low, CI_high]\"。附行均值和列均值。\n\n      '\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Bootstrap CI是paper reporting质量的基本要求，审稿人三档均要求。 主要作用：(1) 证明所有cells统计显著高于chance；\n    (2) topk50的CI可能被reviewer用来argue\"weakest setting接近 baseline\"——但CI下界仍在68%以上； (3)\n    部分cells间CI重叠说明model effect和strategy effect的 大小关系需要在paper中显式讨论。\n\n    '\n- name: theoretical_analysis_section\n  plan_id: plan_023\n  description: '理论分析section：(1) tail erosion连接p90_ppl/var_surprisal, (2) EDD上界推导,\n    (3) strategy-dependent convergence rate解释。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    tail_erosion_connection: qualitative — links p90_ppl dominance to Shumailov 2024\n      tail collapse mechanism\n    edd_upper_bound_formula: EDD ≤ ⌈log(D_KL(P_0 || P_ref) / τ_disc) / log(1/γ)⌉ where\n      γ is contraction rate\n    edd_bound_empirical_match: bound gives EDD≤6 for 1B models, empirical EDD=4 —\n      bound is loose but directionally correct\n    iid_assumption_violation: acknowledged — LoRA recursive chain violates i.i.d.\n      because each depth uses different LoRA weights\n    strategy_convergence_explanation: temperature uniform scaling accelerates KL contraction\n      by factor ~1.3-1.5x vs truncation methods\n    section_length_pages: 1.5\n    contribution_list_included: false\n    section_label: Theoretical Motivation\n  result_rationale: '理论section在median档下仅提供定性连接： (1) Tail erosion连接：Shumailov et al.\n    2024证明recursive training 使模型逐渐丧失对低概率token的生成能力(tail collapse)， 这直接解释了为什么p90_ppl(捕捉高perplexity\n    tail)和var_surprisal (捕捉surprisal分布宽度)是universal top features—— recursive generation系统性地压缩perplexity分布的right\n    tail， 使p90_ppl单调下降。这个连接是直觉性的、定性的，不构成新理论； (2) EDD上界推导：假设recursive generation是contraction\n    mapping (每代分布向attractor收敛，contraction rate γ<1)， EDD是相邻depths的KL divergence首次降至discriminability\n    threshold τ_disc以下的depth。推导得EDD ≤ ⌈log(D_0/τ)/log(1/γ)⌉。 问题：此推导假设i.i.d. generation（每代用同一个generative\n    process）， 但实际实验中每个depth用不同的LoRA checkpoint—— 审稿人会指出\"the bound assumes a fixed\n    contraction operator, but your LoRA fine-tuning creates a different operator at\n    each depth\"； (3) EDD bound给出≤6（1B模型），empirical EDD=4—— bound是loose的但方向正确，审稿人可能认为\"a\n    bound that overestimates by 50% is descriptive rather than tight\"； (4) Strategy\n    convergence rate解释：temperature对logit做uniform scaling (除以τ)保持分布shape但改变entropy，而nucleus/topk做truncation\n    (截断低概率tail)。Temperature使模型更快收敛到uniform-like attractor， 解释了temp09的d1→d2 feature\n    trajectory reversal。 这个解释有mechanistic basis但缺乏formal proof； (5) 整个section约1.5页，标注为\"Theoretical\n    Motivation\"， 不列入contribution list以避免审稿人的\"no theoretical contribution\"critique。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description:\n  - 'EDD bound vs empirical: 柱状图showing theoretical upper bound (6) vs empirical EDD\n    at T=0.75 across 3 models (all=4), 附contraction rate γ估计值'\n  - 'Tail erosion visualization: p90_ppl的empirical CDF across depths (d0-d3), 展示right\n    tail系统性左移, 连接到Shumailov tail collapse theory'\n  analysis: 'Median档下理论section的定位是\"adds motivation but not substance\"。 审稿人典型反应：\"The\n    theoretical sketch is helpful for intuition but the EDD bound relies on assumptions\n    that don''t hold in practice (i.i.d. generation). I appreciate the connection\n    to model collapse theory but would categorize this as ''descriptive'' rather than\n    ''a theoretical contribution''.\" 这意味着理论section不会提升reviewer score，但也不会扣分—— 它防止了\"no\n    theoretical grounding at all\"的批评。 关键是不要oversell：paper说\"we provide theoretical\n    motivation connecting our empirical findings to model collapse theory\" 而非\"we derive\n    novel theoretical results\"。\n\n    '\n- name: api_model_recursive_chains\n  plan_id: plan_026\n  description: 'GPT-4o-mini fine-tuning API递归链 + prompted recursive chain (rewrite模式)，\n    验证depth signal在商用API模型中的存在性。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    prompted_chain_4class_acc: 0.42\n    prompted_chain_d0v1_auc: 0.73\n    prompted_chain_d1v2_auc: 0.57\n    prompted_chain_d2v3_auc: 0.52\n    prompted_chain_top_features:\n    - surprisal_range\n    - prob_std\n    - var_surprisal\n    finetuned_chain_feasibility: limited — API fine-tuning constraints (no LoRA control,\n      fixed epochs) make recursive chain less controlled\n    finetuned_chain_4class_acc: 0.45\n    finetuned_chain_d1v2_auc: 0.59\n    delta_vs_base_1b_pp: -36.0\n    delta_vs_instruct_pp: -3.0\n  result_rationale: 'API模型结果弱于base model，与instruct model实验(plan_021, 47.4%)一致： (1)\n    Prompted recursive chain (rewrite prompting)：每次\"rewrite\"不等同于 LoRA fine-tune——fine-tune改变模型参数使分布永久偏移，\n    prompted rewrite仅在inference时施加instruction bias。 因此递归prompted generation的分布偏移幅度远小于LoRA递归链，\n    导致相邻depth的statistical features差异更小； (2) API fine-tuning (GPT-4o-mini)：OpenAI fine-tuning\n    API不暴露 LoRA rank/learning rate等超参数，默认训练3 epochs且有 内置regularization防止catastrophic\n    forgetting—— 这正是depth signal所需要的分布偏移的对立面。 递归fine-tune在API上产生的每代偏移可能仅为本地LoRA的30-40%；\n    (3) RLHF/instruction tuning引入的分布约束(alignment tax) 使模型生成更\"standardized\"——不同depth的生成在style/fluency上更一致，\n    压缩了statistical feature的variance； (4) Feature ranking偏移：p90_ppl不再dominant(被surprisal_range替代)，\n    因为API模型的perplexity tail被RLHF regularize过， tail erosion信号被alignment process预先消除；\n    (5) 42-45%的accuracy仍高于chance(25%)，说明signal exists but is weak—— 这支撑\"depth signal\n    is strongest in base models at moderate scale\" 的bounded claim。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Table_model_type_comparison\n    description: '行=模型类型(Base 1B avg / Base 14B / Instruct 1.5B / API prompted / API\n      finetuned), 列=4class acc / d1v2 AUC / d0v1 AUC / top feature。 展示signal strength随model\n      regularization递减的gradient。\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Signal strength gradient: 条形图showing 4-class acc across model types (base→instruct→API),\n    展示从78%→47%→42%的递减趋势'\n  analysis: 'API模型结果确认\"depth signal is a property of base model generation that is\n    attenuated by instruction tuning and RLHF alignment\"。 论文framing：depth estimation\n    is most applicable to base model outputs in data feedback loops (the primary use\n    case), while instruct/API model chains show attenuated but non-zero signal. 审稿人可能将此解读为limitation(\"only\n    works well on base models\") 或strength(\"correctly identifies that aligned models\n    resist distributional drift\")——取决于reviewer perspective。 Median档下至少一位审稿人会用这个结果argue\n    \"practical impact is limited since most real-world synthetic text comes from instruct/API\n    models\"。\n\n    '\n- name: dcol_component_ablation\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: DCOL组件消融实验——已取消，因前置条件plan_004(DCOL v6)结论为negative。\n  expected_results:\n    status: cancelled\n    reason: DCOL v6 RoBERTa-large failed (64.4% vs RF 78.2%, -13.7pp, severe overfitting).\n      No DCOL model to ablate.\n  result_rationale: 'DCOL v1-v6全部失败表明contrastive ordinal learning在text depth estimation\n    任务上有固有困难：(1) 文本的ordinal depth signal主要编码在statistical features (perplexity tail,\n    surprisal variance)中，而非token-level embeddings能直接捕捉的； (2) contrastive loss需要embedding空间中adjacent\n    depths有清晰的ordinal structure， 但RoBERTa的[CLS] embedding捕捉的是语义信息而非distributional\n    statistics； (3) 这个negative result本身支持Atlas/EDD作为primary contribution的定位—— 表明depth\n    estimation的贡献在于feature discovery和task formalization， 而非novel deep learning architecture。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Plan_010取消不影响论文结构。DCOL negative result已纳入paper的 negative analysis section\n    (Section 5或Appendix)， 作为\"contrastive ordinal learning的固有局限\"discussion。\n\n    '\n- name: theory_section_whatif\n  plan_id: what_if:theory_section\n  description: '与plan_023重叠的theoretical analysis what-if。 在median档下评估其对reviewer score的marginal\n    impact。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    marginal_score_impact: +0.0 to +0.25\n    reviewer_perception: appreciated as motivation, not counted as contribution\n    best_case: reviewer says 'nice connection to theory, strengthens the empirical\n      narrative'\n    worst_case: reviewer says 'the theoretical analysis is superficial and the EDD\n      bound is too loose to be useful'\n    champion_reviewer_probability: 0.35\n  result_rationale: '理论section在median档的marginal impact接近零到微正： (1) 正面场景(+0.25)：某位reviewer认可problem\n    formalization +  theoretical motivation的组合，认为\"this paper doesn''t need novel theory\n    to be valuable — the empirical contribution is sufficient, and the theoretical\n    sketch adds context\"； (2) 中性场景(+0.0)：reviewer认为理论section是nice-to-have但 不改变evaluation——\"the\n    theory section provides some intuition but doesn''t affect my assessment of the\n    empirical claims\"； (3) 微负场景(-0.1)：aggressive reviewer认为理论section raises expectations\n    it doesn''t meet——\"including a ''theory'' section suggests the authors believe\n    they have a theoretical contribution, but the analysis is too informal to qualify\"。\n    Median档的结果是(2)或(1)，取决于reviewer composition。 Champion reviewer(认可formalization价值)的概率约35%——\n    需要恰好分配到有empirical study appreciation的reviewer。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: Theory section是low-risk low-reward的addition。 在median档下它不会pushing the paper\n    from 3.0 to 3.5， 但也不会hurt。其主要价值是在rebuttal中当reviewer问 \"why these features?\"时可以指向theory\n    section作为解释。 建议：保留theory section但严格控制scope和claim， 明确标注为\"Theoretical Motivation\"并在Introduction的\n    contribution list中不单独列出。\n","numLines":410,"startLine":1,"totalLines":410}}}
